content:
You build UI for our product. Follow this design brief exactly.

Playbook components are available: import them as `import { Button } from "@/components/Button"` (same for every component name). Do not re-implement them.

# Design brief: Build a pricing page with three plans (Solo, Team, Business), a monthly/yearly toggle, a feature comparison and an FAQ.

Playbook: **Almanac** — Sample playbook: an editorial, paper-and-ink system. Flat surfaces, hairline borders, one warm accent. Replace with your own.

## Voice

Almanac reads like a well-set printed ledger, not a SaaS template.

- **Flat, not floaty.** No shadows, no gradients, no glassmorphism. Depth comes from hairline `line` borders and the `paper-2` recessed surface.
- **Whitespace over dividers.** Separate groups with space (24-48px) before reaching for a border.
- **Type does the hierarchy.** Fraunces for titles and hero numbers, Plex Sans for everything else. Don't use colour or boxes to create emphasis that size and weight could create.
- **One accent, used sparingly.** `accent` marks the single most important action on a screen and the active state. If everything is orange, nothing is.
- **Dense but calm.** Tables and lists are compact (12-16px row padding); page margins are generous (48-64px on desktop).
- **Left-aligned.** Content hangs from a left edge. Centred layouts only for empty states and auth.
- **Numbers are tabular.** Money, counts and IDs use `font-mono` so columns line up.
- **Copy is plain.** Sentence case everywhere. Buttons are verbs ("Save changes", not "Submit"). No exclamation marks.

## Hard rules (the checker enforces these)

- **Only palette colours.** Use a palette token: bg-paper, text-ink-2, border-line, bg-accent...
- **No arbitrary Tailwind values.** Pick the nearest token from the scale.
- **Spacing from the scale only.** p-5 (20px) → p-4 or p-6. gap-10 (40px) → gap-8 or gap-12.
- **Font sizes from the type scale.** Use text-xs, text-sm, text-base, text-lg, text-xl, text-2xl or text-3xl.
- **Fraunces, Plex Sans, Plex Mono only.** font-display for titles, font-body for text, font-mono for numbers.
- **Radius: none, sm (2), md (6), full.** Cards and inputs: rounded-md. Badges: rounded-full. Tables: rounded-none.
- **No shadows.** Replace shadow-* with border border-line.
- **No gradients.** Use a single palette fill.
- **Use playbook components.** Import Button, Field, DataTable, etc. from the components folder.
- **No inline style values.** Use token classes.
- **Images need alt text.** Add alt="..." (alt="" for decorative).
- **Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (3:1 for large text).** Use ink / ink-2 / ink-3 on paper surfaces, accent-ink on accent.
- **No horizontal scroll at 375px.** Stack columns below md:, let tables scroll inside their own container.
- At most one primary button per view (warning). Demote the others to variant="secondary" or "ghost".
- One h1, no skipped heading levels (warning). h1 → h2 → h3 in order.

## Tokens (Tailwind class names in backticks)

Colours:
- `paper` #F4F1EA — Page background. The default surface. Never use pure white.
- `paper-2` #EAE5D9 — Recessed surface: table header, hover fill, sidebar.
- `ink` #1B1A17 — Primary text, strong borders, secondary button outline.
- `ink-2` #4D4A42 — Body copy and labels.
- `ink-3` #66625A — Meta text: timestamps, helper text, captions.
- `line` #D6D0C2 — Hairline dividers and card borders.
- `accent` #B8401A — The single call-to-action colour. Primary button, active nav, focus ring.
- `accent-ink` #F4F1EA — Text on accent fills.
- `moss` #2F6B4F — Success / positive deltas.
- `ochre` #8A5F12 — Warning / pending.
- `brick` #9E3326 — Error / destructive / negative deltas.

Fonts:
- `font-display` Fraunces — Page titles, section headings, big numbers. Weights 500-600.
- `font-body` IBM Plex Sans — Everything else. Weights 400 and 500 only.
- `font-mono` IBM Plex Mono — Tabular numbers, IDs, code, keyboard hints.

Type scale: `text-xs` 12px, `text-sm` 14px, `text-base` 16px, `text-lg` 20px, `text-xl` 28px, `text-2xl` 40px, `text-3xl` 56px
Spacing scale: 0=0px, 1=4px, 2=8px, 3=12px, 4=16px, 6=24px, 8=32px, 12=48px, 16=64px, 24=96px (use only these numbers in p-/m-/gap-/space-)
Radius: `rounded-none` 0px, `rounded-sm` 2px, `rounded-md` 6px, `rounded-full` pill
Shadows: none — do not use shadow-*

## Pattern: Settings page

Page header, then stacked Cards, one per topic, each with Fields and a right-aligned secondary save. Danger zone last.

Skeleton:
```tsx
<main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12">
  <PageHeader/>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <Card title="Profile"> <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">Field...</div> <footer class="mt-6 flex justify-end"><Button/></footer></Card>
    <Card title="Danger zone"> <Button variant="danger"/></Card>
  </div>
</main>
```

Rhythm: Max width 768px. 32px between cards, 24px between fields, 24px above card footers.

Approved exemplar: `exemplars/settings.html` (render it to see the target look).

## Components to use (import from the playbook's components folder; do not re-create them)

### PageHeader

Top of every page: optional mono eyebrow, Fraunces h1, description, actions on the right. Owns the page's only h1.

Props: `eyebrow?: string; title: string; description?: string; actions?: ReactNode`
Do: Put the page's primary Button here
Don't: A second h1 elsewhere on the page

```tsx
import type { ReactNode } from "react";

export function PageHeader({ eyebrow, title, description, actions }: { eyebrow?: string; title: string; description?: string; actions?: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <header className="mb-12 flex flex-col gap-4 border-b border-line pb-6 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between">
      <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
        {eyebrow && <span className="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-3">{eyebrow}</span>}
        <h1 className="font-display text-2xl font-medium text-ink md:text-3xl">{title}</h1>
        {description && <p className="max-w-prose font-body text-base text-ink-2">{description}</p>}
      </div>
      {actions && <div className="flex gap-3">{actions}</div>}
    </header>
  );
}
```

### Button

The only clickable action. Variants: primary (accent, max one per view), secondary (ink outline, the default), ghost (tertiary), danger (destructive).

Props: `variant?: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost'|'danger'; size?: 'sm'|'md'`
Do: Label with a verb: "Save changes"; Put the primary action last (rightmost) in a button group
Don't: Two primary buttons on one screen; A raw <button> or a styled <a> pretending to be a button

```tsx
import type { ButtonHTMLAttributes } from "react";

type Variant = "primary" | "secondary" | "ghost" | "danger";
type Size = "sm" | "md";

const variants: Record<Variant, string> = {
  primary: "bg-accent text-accent-ink border border-accent hover:bg-ink hover:border-ink",
  secondary: "bg-paper text-ink border border-ink hover:bg-paper-2",
  ghost: "bg-transparent text-ink-2 border border-transparent hover:text-ink hover:border-line",
  danger: "bg-paper text-brick border border-brick hover:bg-paper-2",
};

const sizes: Record<Size, string> = {
  sm: "h-8 px-3 gap-2 text-sm",
  md: "h-12 px-4 gap-2 text-base",
};

export interface ButtonProps extends ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: Variant;
  size?: Size;
}

export function Button({ variant = "secondary", size = "md", className = "", ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button
      className={`inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md font-body font-medium transition-colors focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent disabled:opacity-50 disabled:pointer-events-none ${variants[variant]} ${sizes[size]} ${className}`}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}
```

### Card

A bordered group of related content with an optional title and header action. Flat, 1px line border, 24px padding.

Props: `title?: string; action?: ReactNode`
Do: Use for distinct groups (a settings section, a chart)
Don't: Nest cards inside cards; Add a shadow or rounded-xl

```tsx
import type { HTMLAttributes, ReactNode } from "react";

export interface CardProps extends HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement> {
  title?: string;
  action?: ReactNode;
}

export function Card({ title, action, children, className = "", ...props }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <section className={`rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-6 ${className}`} {...props}>
      {(title || action) && (
        <header className="mb-4 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
          {title && <h2 className="font-display text-lg font-medium text-ink">{title}</h2>}
          {action}
        </header>
      )}
      {children}
    </section>
  );
}
```

### Field

Labelled text input with hint and error text. Label above, 48px tall, accent focus ring.

Props: `label: string; hint?: string; error?: string; + input attributes`
Do: Always pass a visible label; Show errors under the field, in brick
Don't: Placeholder-as-label; Raw <input>

```tsx
import type { InputHTMLAttributes } from "react";
import { useId } from "react";

export interface FieldProps extends InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {
  label: string;
  hint?: string;
  error?: string;
}

export function Field({ label, hint, error, className = "", ...props }: FieldProps) {
  const id = useId();
  return (
    <div className={`flex flex-col gap-2 ${className}`}>
      <label htmlFor={id} className="font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink">{label}</label>
      <input
        id={id}
        aria-invalid={!!error}
        aria-describedby={hint || error ? `${id}-note` : undefined}
        className={`h-12 rounded-md border bg-paper px-3 font-body text-base text-ink placeholder:text-ink-3 focus:outline focus:outline-2 focus:outline-offset-1 focus:outline-accent ${error ? "border-brick" : "border-line"}`}
        {...props}
      />
      {(error || hint) && (
        <p id={`${id}-note`} className={`font-body text-sm ${error ? "text-brick" : "text-ink-3"}`}>{error ?? hint}</p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Badge

Outlined pill for status. Tones: neutral, positive (moss), warning (ochre), negative (brick), accent.

Props: `tone?: 'neutral'|'positive'|'warning'|'negative'|'accent'`
Do: One or two words, sentence case
Don't: Filled colour backgrounds

### SideNav

App sidebar on paper-2 with product name and links; active item marked with an accent left rule.

Props: `product: string; items: {label, href, active?, count?}[]`
Do: Collapse to a top bar below md
Don't: Icons-only navigation; Accent-filled active item

Also available if needed: StatTile (A key number with label, delta and caption); DataTable (Compact table: ink top/bottom rule, paper-2 header, hairline rows, mono numerals right-aligned); EmptyState (Centred, dashed-border placeholder for empty lists with title, one sentence and one action).

## Before you finish

Run the `check` tool on every file you wrote and fix every error it reports. Repeat until it passes.

```tsx
import { useState } from "react";
import { PageHeader } from "@/components/PageHeader";
import { Button } from "@/components/Button";
import { Card } from "@/components/Card";
import { Badge } from "@/components/Badge";
import { DataTable } from "@/components/DataTable";

type BillingPeriod = "monthly" | "yearly";

interface Plan {
  name: string;
  description: string;
  monthlyPrice: number;
  yearlyPrice: number;
  features: string[];
  cta: string;
  popular?: boolean;
}

const plans: Plan[] = [
  {
    name: "Solo",
    description: "For individuals and side projects",
    monthlyPrice: 12,
    yearlyPrice: 10,
    features: [
      "Unlimited projects",
      "10 GB storage",
      "Basic analytics",
      "Email support",
      "API access",
    ],
    cta: "Start free trial",
  },
  {
    name: "Team",
    description: "For small teams shipping together",
    monthlyPrice: 36,
    yearlyPrice: 30,
    features: [
      "Everything in Solo",
      "5 team members",
      "100 GB storage",
      "Advanced analytics",
      "Priority support",
      "SSO authentication",
      "Audit logs",
    ],
    cta: "Start free trial",
    popular: true,
  },
  {
    name: "Business",
    description: "For companies with compliance needs",
    monthlyPrice: 120,
    yearlyPrice: 100,
    features: [
      "Everything in Team",
      "Unlimited members",
      "1 TB storage",
      "Custom analytics",
      "Dedicated support",
      "SLA guarantee",
      "On-premise option",
      "Custom contracts",
    ],
    cta: "Contact sales",
  },
];

const features = [
  { feature: "Projects", solo: "Unlimited", team: "Unlimited", business: "Unlimited" },
  { feature: "Team members", solo: "1", team: "5", business: "Unlimited" },
  { feature: "Storage", solo: "10 GB", team: "100 GB", business: "1 TB" },
  { feature: "Analytics", solo: "Basic", team: "Advanced", business: "Custom" },
  { feature: "Support", solo: "Email", team: "Priority", business: "Dedicated" },
  { feature: "API access", solo: "Yes", team: "Yes", business: "Yes" },
  { feature: "SSO", solo: "No", team: "Yes", business: "Yes" },
  { feature: "Audit logs", solo: "No", team: "Yes", business: "Yes" },
  { feature: "SLA", solo: "No", team: "No", business: "Yes" },
  { feature: "On-premise", solo: "No", team: "No", business: "Yes" },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Can I switch plans later?",
    answer: "Yes, you can upgrade or downgrade at any time. Upgrades take effect immediately, and downgrades apply at the end of your current billing period.",
  },
  {
    question: "What payment methods do you accept?",
    answer: "We accept all major credit cards, ACH transfers, and wire transfers for annual Business plans. Invoices are available for yearly commitments.",
  },
  {
    question: "Is there a free trial?",
    answer: "Solo and Team plans include a 14-day free trial. No credit card required to start. Business plans require a demo call to evaluate fit.",
  },
  {
    question: "What happens when my trial ends?",
    answer: "You'll be prompted to choose a plan and enter payment details. If you don't upgrade, your account will be paused but your data is preserved for 90 days.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do you offer discounts for nonprofits or education?",
    answer: "Yes, we offer 50% off for qualified nonprofits and educational institutions. Contact sales with your organization details to apply.",
  },
];

export default function PricingPage() {
  const [period, setPeriod] = useState<BillingPeriod>("monthly");
  const [openFaq, setOpenFaq] = useState<number | null>(null);

  const getPrice = (plan: Plan) => period === "monthly" ? plan.monthlyPrice : plan.yearlyPrice;
  const getPeriodLabel = () => period === "monthly" ? "/month" : "/year";

  return (
    <main className="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-12">
      <PageHeader
        title="Pricing"
        description="Simple, transparent pricing. No hidden fees. All plans include a 14-day free trial."
      />

      {/* Billing Toggle */}
      <div className="mb-12 flex items-center justify-center gap-4">
        <span className={`font-body text-sm text-${period === "monthly" ? "ink" : "ink-3"}`}>Monthly</span>
        <div className="inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-line bg-paper-2 p-1">
          <Button
            variant={period === "monthly" ? "primary" : "ghost"}
            size="sm"
            onClick={() => setPeriod("monthly")}
            className="rounded-sm"
          >
            Monthly
          </Button>
          <Button
            variant={period === "yearly" ? "primary" : "ghost"}
            size="sm"
            onClick={() => setPeriod("yearly")}
            className="rounded-sm"
          >
            Yearly
            <Badge tone="positive" className="ml-1">Save 17%</Badge>
          </Button>
        </div>
        <span className={`font-body text-sm text-${period === "yearly" ? "ink" : "ink-3"}`}>Yearly</span>
      </div>

      {/* Plan Cards */}
      <div className="mb-16 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {plans.map((plan, index) => (
          <Card
            key={plan.name}
            className={`flex flex-col ${plan.popular ? "border-accent relative" : ""}`}
          >
            {plan.popular && (
              <div className="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2">
                <Badge tone="accent">Most popular</Badge>
              </div>
            )}
            <header className="mb-6">
              <h3 className="font-display text-lg font-medium text-ink">{plan.name}</h3>
              <p className="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-ink-2">{plan.description}</p>
            </header>
            <div className="mb-6 flex items-baseline gap-1">
              <span className="font-mono text-3xl font-medium text-ink tabular-nums">${getPrice(plan)}</span>
              <span className="font-body text-base text-ink-2">{getPeriodLabel()}</span>
              {period === "yearly" && (
                <span className="ml-2 font-body text-xs text-moss">Billed ${getPrice(plan) * 12}/year</span>
              )}
            </div>
            <ul className="mb-8 flex-1 space-y-3" role="list">
              {plan.features.map((feature, i) => (
                <li key={i} className="flex items-start gap-3 font-body text-sm text-ink-2">
                  <svg className="mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 size-5 text-moss" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path fillRule="evenodd" d="M16.707 5.293a1 1 0 010 1.414l-8 8a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 011.414-1.414L8 12.586l7.293-7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0z" clipRule="evenodd" />
                  </svg>
                  {feature}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <footer>
              <Button
                variant={plan.popular ? "primary" : "secondary"}
                className="w-full"
                size="md"
              >
                {plan.cta}
              </Button>
            </footer>
          </Card>
        ))}
      </div>

      {/* Feature Comparison */}
      <section className="mb-16" aria-labelledby="comparison-heading">
        <h2 id="comparison-heading" className="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink mb-6">Feature comparison</h2>
        <div className="overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-line">
          <DataTable
            columns={[
              { key: "feature", header: "Feature", className: "font-body text-sm text-ink-2 w-48" },
              { key: "solo", header: "Solo", className: "font-body text-sm text-ink text-center" },
              { key: "team", header: "Team", className: "font-body text-sm text-ink text-center" },
              { key: "business", header: "Business", className: "font-body text-sm text-ink text-center" },
            ]}
            rows={features}
            keyField="feature"
            renderCell={(row, col) => {
              if (col.key === "feature") {
                return <span className="font-body text-sm text-ink-2">{row.feature}</span>;
              }
              const value = row[col.key as keyof typeof row] as string;
              const isYes = value === "Yes";
              const isNo = value === "No";
              const isUnlimited = value === "Unlimited";
              return (
                <span className={`font-body text-sm ${isYes ? "text-moss" : isNo ? "text-ink-3" : "text-ink"}`}>
                  {isYes ? (
                    <svg className="mx-auto size-5 text-moss" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                      <path fillRule="evenodd" d="M16.707 5.293a1 1 0 010 1.414l-8 8a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 011.414-1.414L8 12.586l7.293-7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0z" clipRule="evenodd" />
                    </svg>
                  ) : isNo ? (
                    <svg className="mx-auto size-5 text-ink-3" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
                      <path fillRule="evenodd" d="M4.293 4.293a1 1 0 011.414 0L10 8.586l4.293-4.293a1 1 0 111.414 1.414L11.414 10l4.293 4.293a1 1 0 01-1.414 1.414L10 11.414l-4.293 4.293a1 1 0 01-1.414-1.414L8.586 10 4.293 5.707a1 1 0 010-1.414z" clipRule="evenodd" />
                    </svg>
                  ) : (
                    value
                  )}
                </span>
              );
            }}
          />
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* FAQ */}
      <section aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
        <h2 id="faq-heading" className="font-display text-xl font-medium text-ink mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div className="space-y-3">
          {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
            <Card key={index} className="overflow-hidden">
              <button
                type="button"
                onClick={() => setOpenFaq(openFaq === index ? null : index)}
                className="w-full flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-0 text-left focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent"
                aria-expanded={openFaq === index}
              >
                <h3 className="font-display text-base font-medium text-ink px-6 py-4">{faq.question}</h3>
                <svg
                  className={`flex-shrink-0 size-5 text-ink-3 transition-transform ${openFaq === index ? "rotate-180" : ""}`}
                  viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                  fill="currentColor"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                >
                  <path d="M5.293 7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0L10 10.586l3.293-3.293a1 1 0 111.414 1.414l-4 4a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 010-1.414z" />
                </svg>
              </button>
              {openFaq === index && (
                <div className="border-t border-line bg-paper-2 px-6 pb-4">
                  <p className="font-body text-sm text-ink-2">{faq.answer}</p>
                </div>
              )}
            </Card>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  );
}
```
